1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,540
Hi, I'm Jonathan Reibach. My presentation
was on DIDWebs and the connection between

2
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:12,000
KERI and the decentralized identifier
ecosystem. Well, I think KERI offers some

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,860
unique qualities that really help DIDWebs
be the strongest version of the DIDWeb

4
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:27,860
family of identifiers. Specifically, it
allows for the controller to explicitly

5
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:33,820
authorize information like host
information, path information. And it also

6
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:38,840
allows for much more convenience when
dealing with very, very long-lived

7
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:44,380
identifiers like over the span of decades,
